guide.orespawn.biomes.title=Biomes
guide.orespawn.biomes.1=Provider mods can offer new biomes. Augment mixes them with the existing world, while Replace uses only the configured choices where the rule applies.
guide.orespawn.biomes.2=Scope decides which existing biome namespaces can be replaced. Minecraft Only protects every modded biome; Selected Mods changes only namespaces you choose.
guide.orespawn.biomes.3=Region Size controls broad patches. Each biome can use weight, climate limits, similar-biome hints, and optional top, filler, underwater, and ceiling blocks.
guide.orespawn.patterns.title=Ore Shapes and Visibility
guide.orespawn.patterns.1=Compact makes familiar blobs. Veins stretch through rock, Clusters form groups, Clouds spread broadly, and Under Fluids favours blocks beneath liquids.
guide.orespawn.patterns.2=Height Distribution controls where attempts land between Minimum and Maximum Y. Uniform spreads them evenly; triangle choices favour particular depths.
guide.orespawn.patterns.3=Air-Exposure Discard hides some ore touching caves. 0 keeps every exposed attempt and 1 rejects all exposed attempts; values between are chances.
guide.orespawn.fluids.title=Fluid Deposits
guide.orespawn.fluids.1=Fluid Deposits create covered underground pockets of water, lava, oil, or another installed fluid. They are separate from oceans and World Materials.
guide.orespawn.fluids.2=Attempts per Chunk controls rarity. Horizontal and Vertical Radius set deposit size, while Lobes join several rounded pockets into a less regular shape.
guide.orespawn.fluids.3=Solid Cover protects the roof and Solid Shell protects the sides and floor from caves. Hosts and biome rules decide where a deposit is allowed.
guide.orespawn.materials.title=World Materials
guide.orespawn.materials.1=World Materials changes background materials across a whole dimension. Use Fluid Deposits instead when you only want occasional underground pockets.
guide.orespawn.materials.2=Aquifer Fluid changes the normal fluid used below sea level. Deep Aquifer uses a second fluid below the chosen Y level.
guide.orespawn.materials.3=Snow and Ice replace vanilla snow and ordinary ice near the surface. Not set leaves Minecraft's normal material unchanged.
